   "id": "Add.add",
   "docstring": "`a + b` computes the sum of `a` and `b`. See `HAdd`. "},
  {"signature": "{α : Type u} → (α → α → α) → Add α",
   "module": "Init.Prelude",
   "kind": "constructor",
   "id": "Add.mk",
   "docstring": ""},
  {"signature": "ℕ → ℕ → ℕ",
   "module": "Init.Prelude",
   "kind": "definition",
   "id": "Nat.add",
   "docstring":
   "Addition of natural numbers, typically used via the `+` operator.\n\nThis function is overridden in both the kernel and the compiler to efficiently evaluate using the\narbitrary-precision arithmetic library. The definition provided here is the logical model.\n"},
  {"signature": "{motive : ℕ → Sort u} → ℕ → Sort (max 1 u)",
   "module": "Init.Prelude",
   "kind": "definition",
   "id": "Nat.below",
   "docstring": ""},
